      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The core tension is whether the Second Amendment guarantees an absolute right to bear arms, which Originalists argue based on the text's historical meaning. Conversely, the Living Constitution approach argues that the amendment's meaning must evolve with modern society and technology, allowing for greater judicial flexibility. Originalists insist the Founders intended a specific, limited right, while proponents of the Living Constitution believe the right must adapt to contemporary threats and needs.",
